{
  "goal": "A 5 V USB-C powered running light. An NE555 makes a clock of about 2 Hz, a CD4017 decade counter steps through ten outputs, and each output lights one red LED. Two ICs only.",
  "agreed": [
    {
      "topic": "Function",
      "text": "Ten red LEDs light one at a time in a loop, a running light. About 2 steps per second.",
      "by": "student",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "ts": "2026-10-18T20:01:50"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Power",
      "text": "USB-C, 5 V only. J1 has VBUS, GND, CC1 and CC2; R4 and R5 (5.1k) on CC1/CC2 make the charger give 5 V. C5 10uF on VBUS.",
      "by": "student",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "ts": "2026-10-18T20:01:50"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Clock",
      "text": "U1 NE555 astable: f = 1.44 / ((R1 + 2*R2) * C1) = 1.44 / (146k * 4.7uF), about 2.1 Hz. C2 10nF on CTRL.",
      "by": "student",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "ts": "2026-10-18T20:01:50"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Counter and LEDs",
      "text": "U2 CD4017 counts the clock and raises Q0..Q9 in turn, each driving one LED anode. All cathodes share R3 470R to GND, so one LED is on at a time (about 7 mA).",
      "by": "student",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "ts": "2026-10-18T20:01:50"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Board",
      "text": "Two layers, 0603/0805 parts, SOIC-8 and SOIC-16 for the two ICs. One 100nF decoupling cap per IC.",
      "by": "student",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "ts": "2026-10-18T20:01:50"
    }
  ],
